e1's pre-existing docker0 address) was left unreverted but caused no observed functional harm.\",\"limitations\":[\"The docker0 address/state change on node1 (cmd-2b2b6e8caf204249) has no clear task justification and was not reverted, though its practical impact appears negligible.\",\"Post-reboot docker ps on node1 was captured only 2 seconds after boot, showing just the 'database' container up; full container stack health at steady state was not separately re-verified, though later successful pings imply routing-relevant kernel forwarding was sufficient regardless of container state.\",\"before_prepare and after_prepare snapshots are identical (prepare phase was disabled), so preparer- vs executor-caused changes could only be distinguished via the after_executor comparison, which is consistent with the executor's own timeline.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"node1 (SONiC) is given a routed interface inside each VLAN (eth1 in the node2 VLAN, eth2 in the node3 VLAN) with appropriate addressing","status":"satisfied","summary":"node1 eth1 assigned 192.168.10.1/24 and eth2 assigned 192.168.20.1/24, confirmed via ip addr show both before and after a full reboot, with config persisted in /etc/network/interfaces.d/eth1 and eth2.","evidence_ids":["cmd-71bf4b291cad4ebc","cmd-3ee30dd211124676","cmd-0383ce66da9d4e6e"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"node1 forwards IPv4 traffic between the two VLAN-facing interfaces","status":"satisfied","summary":"net.ipv4.ip_forward and per-interface forwarding for eth1/eth2 set to 1, persisted via /etc/sysctl.d/99-antrieb.conf, and verified intact after node1's reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-71bf4b291cad4ebc","cmd-3ee30dd211124676","cmd-0383ce66da9d4e6e"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"node2 and node3 are addressed within their own VLAN subnets and have routes to the other VLAN via node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"node2 eth1=192.168.10.2/24 with a static route to 192.168.20.0/24 via 192.168.10.1; node3 eth1=1